= Vilnius Question

On 20 February 1922, the Seimas of Central Lithuania adopted a resolution declaring the Vilnius Region an inseparable part of the Republic of Poland. The motion passed by 96 votes to none, with six abstentions, rejecting all foreign claims to the territory and requesting its immediate incorporation into the Polish state.

*“The Vilnius Land constitutes, without conditions or reservations, an inseparable part of the Republic of Poland”* — Point 4 of the resolution

